umiproc patch 0003: no inertial edge across a relocalization (localization against a loaded map)

What: Tracking::Track, INIT_RELOCALIZE success (the first relocalization against a loaded map and every later
one after tracking fails). For an inertial sensor the new keyframe gets no preintegration (nullptr), the
current frame too (it is that keyframe), the frame's last keyframe is that keyframe, and a fresh
mpImuPreintegratedFromLastKF starts from it (its bias, the IMU calibration). The old preintegration object is
not deleted: earlier Frame copies still point to it.
Why: the keyframe copied the tracker's running preintegration, i.e. the IMU since the start of the run (first
relocalization) or since the last keyframe before tracking was lost, and that same object then also became the
next keyframe's preintegration (CreateNewKeyFrame hands the running object to the next keyframe). So
LocalInertialBA linked the mapping run's last keyframe (or the keyframe before the loss) to the relocalized
keyframe with IMU that does not belong to that interval, as a non-robust edge once the map has passed VIBA 2,
and PoseInertialOptimizationLastKeyFrame used the same over-long preintegration.
What the optimizers then do with that keyframe (the fork's existing null guards, the same path the fork already
takes when relocalization succeeds on frame 0, which has no IMU samples): LocalInertialBA skips its inertial
and bias random-walk edges to the previous keyframe ("No IMU Preintegration for KeyFrame N, skipping inertial
edge."); its pose is held by its visual edges; its velocity and bias vertices have no edge until the next
keyframe exists, so g2o leaves them out of the optimisation; the next keyframe's edge (IMU integrated from the
relocalized frame) then links the two correctly. FullInertialBA, InertialOptimization, MergeInertialBA and
InitializeIMU skip it the same way; KeyFrameCulling never removes it (or its predecessor while it is the next
keyframe), so the keyframe chain stays intact.
Behaviour change: localization runs whose relocalization succeeds after frame 0, or that relocalize again
later. A relocalization on frame 0 is unchanged apart from the bias the fresh preintegration starts from.

diff --git a/src/Tracking.cc b/src/Tracking.cc
index 01e7881..beb6781 100644
--- a/src/Tracking.cc
+++ b/src/Tracking.cc
@@ -1660,6 +1660,18 @@ void Tracking::Track()
                     if (bOK) { 
                         cout << "INIT_RELOCALIZE success!" << endl;
                         KeyFrame* pKFcur = new KeyFrame(mCurrentFrame,mpAtlas->GetCurrentMap(),mpKeyFrameDB);
+                        if(mSensor==System::IMU_MONOCULAR || mSensor==System::IMU_STEREO || mSensor==System::IMU_RGBD)
+                        {
+                            // umiproc patch 0003: no inertial link across a relocalization. The keyframe used to copy
+                            // the running preintegration (IMU since the start of the run or the last keyframe, which
+                            // the next keyframe then shared), so the edge to the previous keyframe spanned unrelated
+                            // IMU. Now it has none (the optimizers skip a keyframe without one, as after frame 0), and
+                            // the IMU is integrated afresh from here. The old object is left alone (frames use it).
+                            pKFcur->mpImuPreintegrated = nullptr;
+                            mCurrentFrame.mpImuPreintegrated = nullptr;
+                            mCurrentFrame.mpLastKeyFrame = pKFcur;
+                            mpImuPreintegratedFromLastKF = new IMU::Preintegrated(pKFcur->GetImuBias(),pKFcur->mImuCalib);
+                        }
 
                         // update prev and next pointers
                         vector<KeyFrame*> vpKFs = pCurrentMap->GetAllKeyFrames();
